# General Coding Guidelines

- Use TypeScript for all frontend components.  
- Always provide concise comments explaining complex logic.  
- Prioritize readability and maintainability.
- Use Stripe for billing.
- Do not prompt me to run 'npm run dev' it is already running in the terminal.
- Do not use anything other than bootstrap-icons for all icons within the app.
- Keep track of all tasks in the tasks.json file for the AI to execute.
- Never do more than one phase at a time when implementing features as we will do testing after.
- Keep track of the status of the tasks either pending, in-progress, or complete for each task in task.json.
- never ask me to run npm run dev always assume im already doing it manually.
- never run 'npm run dev' in the terminal.
- always refer to the /docs folder when building new features and check for if there are any requirements or rules set up for this feature.
- refer to the SQL documents in /src/utils/supabase/migrations folder for tables and functions.
- when I ask you to do something I need you to break down the task into paarts and only do one or two chnages at a time.
- anytime I use stripe in a file you need to grab it from the utilies folder.